-- title:
--   Specialisation onto the other vertical component forces a crossing
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, a characteristic-zero field $L$ that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((q))$ obtained by adjoining over $L$ the image under the coefficientwise map [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) (induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$) of [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L137) $\subseteq \mathbb{Q}((q))$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A \to L \to K$, and let $j \in K$ be nonzero with image the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) in $L((q))$. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed $A$-algebra field of characteristic $p$, and write $X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ for [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252), the descent of the two-chart model glued from the charts generated by $j$ and by $j^{-1}$. Let $C_1, C_2$ be integral schemes, proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral over $\operatorname{Spec} k$, together with closed immersions $i_\nu \colon C_\nu \to X \times_{\operatorname{Spec} A} \operatorname{Spec} k$ over $\operatorname{Spec} k$ (i.e. composing $i_\nu$ with the second projection gives the structure morphism of $C_\nu$), whose images cover every point of $X \times_{\operatorname{Spec} A} \operatorname{Spec} k$, and assume the fibre product $C_1 \times_{X_k} C_2$ is reduced with exactly $n > 0$ points. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain, $\rho_O \colon A \to O$ a ring map carrying the maximal ideal of $A$ onto that of $O$, and $t \colon O \to k$ with $t \circ \rho_O =$ the structure map $A \to k$; let $bc$ be a morphism $X \times_{\operatorname{Spec} A} \operatorname{Spec} k \to X \times_{\operatorname{Spec} A} \operatorname{Spec} O$ commuting with the first projections and with the second projections up to $\operatorname{Spec}(t)$. The conclusion is the pair of assertions: for every point $c$ of $C_2$, if the image of $c$ under $i_2$ followed by $bc$ lies in the closure of the image under $i_1$ followed by $bc$ of the generic point of $C_1$, then $i_2(c)$ lies in the image of $i_1$; and symmetrically with the roles of $C_1$ and $C_2$ exchanged.
--
--   This records that a point of one component of the geometric special fibre of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ whose image in the model over $O$ specialises into the vertical component carried by the other component must be a crossing point, i.e. lies on both components. It is used in the computation of the ideal sheaves cut out by the two vertical components, in [`ModularCurve.XOneP.isInvertible_comap_ker_and_comap_ker_eq_prod_ofPoint_of_map_maximalIdeal_eq_twoChartModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.isInvertible_comap_ker_and_comap_ker_eq_prod_ofPoint_of_map_maximalIdeal_eq_twoChartModel_x1_mul).
